// ─── What Marta has agreed to ───────────────────────────────────────────────

/// 374,400 USD at 5.25% over thirty years, first payment 2022-10-01. Interest is the building's; the asset's
/// shares decide whose it is.
contract mortgage with first-federal
  loan 374_400 USD on 2022-08-12 at 5.25% over 30y for triplex
  monthly on 1 from checking                   // ▸ 2,067.45 of principal and interest
  escrow 870 USD into escrow                   // 7,840 property tax and 2,600 insurance, over twelve
  from 2022-10-01                              // the first payment: the schedule counts from here, not from the loan's day

contract property-tax with monroe-county
  about 3_920.00 USD yearly on 01-31, 07-31 from escrow #property-tax of triplex   // ✎ 03b2: as elsewhere, a list of dates

contract insurance with state-farm
  2_600 USD yearly on 06-01 from escrow #insurance of triplex
  covers 1y                                    // ? 03c3: `covers the year` or `covers 1y`? here it is from 06-01 for twelve months

/// The building's water and sewer: quarterly, and in Marta's name. The tenants repay their shares.
contract water with rochester-water
  about 600 USD quarterly on 02-10 from checking #utilities of triplex     // ✎ 03b2: `quarterly on 02-10` also fixes the month
  // ✗ 03a4: what the tenants repay is a claim on them: 32.81% and 31.25% of each bill, added to the next rent.
  // It is computed by hand and written as an item on their rent (journal/2026/03.ax).

contract common-electric with national-grid
  about 46 USD monthly on 20 from checking #utilities of triplex

// ── The leases, all through the manager ─────────────────────────────────────
// The rent is paid to the manager, who keeps 8% of it: an item on every occurrence, so the receipt says
// what arrived, and the fee is `- 8%`.

contract lease-b with tenant-b
  1_850 USD monthly on 1 into pm-trust #rent of unit-b
  - 8% #management via elm-pm
  deposit 1_850 USD                            // ? 03c4: held where? §5's `deposit` names no holding; this one is the manager's
  from 2025-07-01 until 2026-06-30

contract lease-c with tenant-c
  1_950 USD monthly on 1 into pm-trust #rent of unit-c
  - 8% #management via elm-pm
  deposit 1_950 USD
  from 2025-09-01 until 2026-08-31

/// A new tenant for unit C, from mid-May, with the first full month free.
contract lease-c2 with tenant-c2
  2_050 USD monthly on 1 into pm-trust #rent of unit-c
  - 8% #management via elm-pm
  deposit 2_050 USD
  from 2026-05-15 until 2027-05-31

// ✗ 03a3: the leases charge 5% of the rent as a late fee after five days. A late fee is a term of the lease and
// the amount follows from it (5% of 1,850.00), yet `check` only says the rent is late and the fee is typed.
// ✗ 03a7: the first month of lease-c2 is 05-15 to 05-31: 17 of 31 days, written as an amount on its occurrence.

// ── What the manager charges besides its 8% ─────────────────────────────────
// A leasing fee of half a month's rent when it places a tenant, and a hundred dollars to renew one. Neither
// recurs on a schedule: they are flows, typed from its statement.
